License: MS-PL; see LICENSE and retained source headers.
This work-in-progress copy is not installable and is not an accelerated WDDM driver.
Changes for the 8.1 ARM32 build check: the newer display-caps extension and rotation Offset0 are gated by NTDDI_VERSION; MmMapIoSpaceEx and ExAllocatePool2 were replaced by 8.1-compatible APIs, with allocation zeroing retained. No device-specific power, PnP resource or GE8300 code is connected. The upstream sample explicitly does not support sleep. Do not install or deploy this build check.
Source whitespace was normalized.
Present-source mapping now validates positive stride, the full pitched source span and command-list allocation arithmetic, and frees the context on MDL or worker-creation failure. The separate `present_bounds.h` is BSD-2-Clause-Patent. Negative-stride support and all device integration remain unfinished.
Present rectangle and move lists are copied into driver-owned memory under SEH before validation, with 32-bit format and valid source/destination bounds required. This is still a build-only adaptation, not a fully validated WDDM driver.
The CPU present path now completes synchronously instead of alternating with a sample worker thread. Rotation dimensions and centered framebuffer bounds are validated before copying. Device power, stop synchronization and GPU integration remain unfinished.
An opt-in GE8300 provider client can attempt contiguous 16 KiB copies and falls back to the CPU path. The opt-in is not validated on hardware or enabled by default.
Concurrent level-zero present calls are serialized with a kernel mutex; mode changes, stop, reset and power transitions still require separate lifecycle verification.
